  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the alert rule exist, and the rule is enabled.\n\n**Data exploration.** The `Kibana Sample Data Logs` view covers 14,074 requests from 1,001 distinct client IPs and 448 URLs. Timestamps run from Oct 4 to Dec 3, 2026. Response codes are only 200 (12,832), 404 (801), and 503 (441). The 5xx total is 441, all of them 503s.\n\n**Dashboard:** `EFF-9e32a607 Web logs overview` (id `eff-9e32a607-web-logs-overview-23bd10445df1`) has four panels:\n- Total requests (metric)\n- Requests by response code (pie)\n- Requests over time by response code (bar, date histogram)\n- 5xx responses (ES|QL metric, `response.keyword LIKE \"5??\"`, currently 441)\n\n**Alert rule:** `EFF-9e32a607 5xx spike` (id `c99fadec-490d-47c0-a0f9-d0e98f8a4f63`) is an `.es-query` rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`, running every 1m. It counts documents where `response.keyword` is between `500` and `599` in the last 5 minutes and fires when the count is greater than 10. It is enabled, and its status is `ok`.\n\nChoices I made that you may want to change:\n- **Dashboard time range:** I set it to Oct 1 \u2013 Dec 31, 2026 because the sample data sits in that window and today is Oct 12. The default last-7-days would show little.\n- **5xx range query:** Kibana's filter syntax has no way to express \"5xx\" directly, so the rule uses a lexicographic range on the keyword field. That works for three-digit codes.\n\nOne thing to be aware of: the rule looks at the last 5 minutes relative to now. The sample data's timestamps extend into the future (to Dec 3), so the rule won't see any of the 441 503s unless new traffic arrives. It is correct, but it may not fire on this data.",
